Comparing different aggregation methods...

Available aggregation strategies:
  - sum
  - weighted

Correlation between aggregation strategies (Control):
           sum weighted
sum      1.000    0.997
weighted 0.997    1.000

Correlation between aggregation strategies (Mutant):
           sum weighted
sum      1.000    0.996
weighted 0.996    1.000

Strategy comparison statistics:
  Control sum range:      0.0 - 2371.1
  Control weighted range: 0.0 - 98.2
  Mutant sum range:       0.1 - 3053.6
  Mutant weighted range:  0.0 - 132.5

✓ Main count matrix uses 'sum' aggregation

Strategy Interpretation:
  - 'sum': Simple sum of all 25 pixels in 5×5 buffer
           → Best for detecting ANY signal in buffer region
           → Robust to positional shifts
           → May include more background noise

  - 'weighted': Distance-weighted sum (center pixels weighted higher)
           → Gives more importance to center pixel
           → Balance between precision and shift-tolerance
           → Values typically lower than sum

✓ High correlation between strategies (>0.95)
  → Choice of aggregation method has minimal impact on results
  → Both strategies capture similar biological signal

